  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 207 AM EST Wed Nov 25 2026\n\nHigh pressure and zonal flow aloft will result in dry and cooler \nthan normal conditions for Friday and Saturday. Attention then turns \nto an upper level low cutting across Mexico which will get absorbed \ninto the larger longwave trough late in the weekend. This trough \nwill swing through the eastern US late in the weekend into early \nnext week. Moisture will increase ahead of an approaching front \nbringing the threat for showers back into the forecast for late \nSunday into early next week. Temperatures will also be on the \nincrease back to around seasonal norms by early next week.",
